    "topic": "The tiny jeans pocket was made for a pocket watch",
    "summary": "Jacob Davis and Levi Strauss patented riveted work pants on May 20, 1873 (US patent 139,121, 'Improvement in Fastening Pocket-Openings'); the 1873 design had two front pockets and one back patch pocket. The small riveted watch pocket was first added by Levi Strauss in the late 1870s. A watch pocket, or fob pocket, is a small compartment originally for holding a pocket watch; it is also called a coin pocket.",
